WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.360 --> 00:00:04.150 align:start position:0%
 
recycling advice and help  good news rochford district council is  pleased to announce that you can now  recycle all food and drink cartons and  all envelopes with and without windows  in your grey recyclables bin the council  has started working with upm who will  sort out all the recyclable material  from the kerbside recyclables  collections  there's a new contract and there are a  few things we'd like to ask you to do to  help make sure it runs smoothly  where possible squash all plastic  bottles and put the lid back on  all lids should be placed back on glass  bottles and jars plastic bottles and  food and drinks cartons  beware your bin may not get emptied if  you have the wrong items in your  recyclables or compostables bin  if you have any black sacs in the  recyclables or compostable spin these  types of bags can only be used in the  non-recyclable bin  or if you have any plastic bags in your  compostables bin the only bags you can  use in this bin are 100 compostable bags  with the seedling logo on them  you can also wrap your food waste in  newspaper or place it in the bin loose  you can place any larger pieces of  cardboard folded down next to your  recyclables bin on the day of your  recycling collection  and don't forget batteries  around 600 million household batteries  are sent to landfill unnecessarily every  year in the uk according to figures from  waste and resources  action program  you can recycle household batteries at  all the libraries council reception  areas in rochford and rayleigh and also  in most schools around the district so  please keep an eye out for the boxes  rodford district council in partnership  with the waste contractor ceta uk  provides a chargeable collection service  of large bulky household furniture and  electrical household items  the charges for the collection of bulky  waste household furniture and electrical  household items are as follows  up to three items 15 pounds and then  it's five pounds per additional item for  items booked at the same time and please  note all items must be booked at the  same time  the furniture collected under the bulky  waste scheme will be taken to landfill  so please think about whether the items  can be reused before you book a  collection  if they're in good condition then you  may wish to consider contacting a  charity shop some of whom may be able to  collect  please check with your local charity  shops before you take any items there to  find your nearest charity shop please  visit the website  www.rochford.gov  dot uk  forward slash recycling  alternatively there are a number of  organizations which reuse your old or  unwanted items these can also be found  in the related links on the website  if you're unable to reuse your item and  wish to arrange collection and payment  please call the customer services on  zero one seven zero two three one eight  one double one during the hours of 8 30  a.m to 5 pm monday to thursday  and 8 30 to 4 30 on fridays  additionally payment can be made by  check payable to rochefort district  council and buy cash at the council  offices in south street rochford and the  civic suite hockley road railing  please note that after a payment has  been made there are no refunds if you  choose to cancel  on the website is a list of the items we  do and do not take however this is not  exhaustive  if there are any items not listed on the  website and you require collection  please call us  you can also email us on customer  services  at rochford.gov dot uk to check if we  could collect the items for you  looking after our local landmarks from  fountains in hockley to post boxes in  ashland rochefort district council want  to know which historic land local  landmarks are important to you  the council is currently seeking your  views as to which buildings you consider  to be local heritage assets or  lhas across the district there are  numerous buildings and items of street  furniture called local heritage assets  which are locally important and  contribute to the character of the area  but are not considered to merit listed  building status following national  guidance and the recognized importance  of retaining and enhancing local built  heritage the council is in the process  of developing a list of those local  heritage assets called the local list  through this list the council will seek  to protect important local heritage  assets by working with owners and other  interested parties  rochford district council's portfolio  holder for planning and transportation  councillor keith hudson said over the  past few years we have lost some  architectural treasures perhaps not  worthy of listed building status but  nevertheless important to the residents  of rochford district  the restoration of the local list will  go some way in affording protection to  our heritage for the benefit of  generations to come  the council has prepared a document for  you to view and have your say which  includes local heritage assets that had  previously been identified in the 1990s  in conjunction with essex county council  and additional suggestions from parish  and town councils  not all of those included in the  consultation document may warrant  inclusion on the local list  the buildings and items of street  furniture in the consultation document  have been assessed against a set of  criteria developed from national  guidance  an important part of the consultation is  to receive views and opinions of the  assessment and additional information  about the history of each entry  the local list consultation document is  available for public viewing and comment  until 6th of may 2011 and may also be  submitted via our online consultation  system at rochford.jd  hyphen consult dot net  forward slash ldf  if you do not have access to the  internet or would like further  information contact the planning policy  team on zero one seven zero two three  one eight one nine one or planning dot  policy at rochefort dot gov dot uk  if you currently hold a bus pass issued  by rochford district council which  expired on the 31st of march  there is no need to complete the contact  the council or complete a renewal  application form  your bus pass should have been  automatically renewed and sent to you  toward the end of march  the design of the new passes has changed  slightly as essex county council is now  responsible for the management of bus  passes within essex although rochford  district council will continue to issue  the passes on behalf of the county  council  there will be no changes to the current  use of the bus pass which will continue  to be between 9 00 am and midnight  monday to friday  and at any time during weekends and  public holidays within essex only  however in all other counties in england  you can use your bus pass from 9 30 a.m  to 11 p.m monday to friday and at any  time during weekends and public holidays  the new bus passes will expire on the  30th of november  2015  for those with surnames beginning from a  to l  for those with surnames beginning with m  to zed the past will expire on the 31st  of march 2016.  and here's some frequently asked  questions with the answers  i've changed my address within the  district since my last bus pass was  issued do i need to notify you  yes  if you have moved and have not already  notified  the council's transportation department  of a change of address your bus pass may  have been sent to your old address  please contact transportation for advice  on zero one two six eight  seven nine eight six zero eight  i now live in the rockford district but  i have a bus pass issued by the previous  authority where i lived  do i need to apply to rochefort for a  new bus pass  if your previous address was in south  end thorac or anywhere else in the  country then yes  you must contact rochford district  council and complete a bus pass  application form you must also contact  your previous authority to advise them  to cancel your bus paths  however  if you lived anywhere else within essex  there is no need for your bus pass to be  replaced as rochwood district council  issued the passes to all residents on  behalf of essex county council  you must however contact rochwood  district council to advise them of your  change of address for their records  my partner relative or close friend has  recently passed away  should i contact the council and return  their bus pass for cancellation  yes  you should contact the council and  return the bus pass as soon as possible  for cancellation  i am no longer able to use my bus pass  should i inform the council that i do  not require a renewal  yes  you should contact the council and  return your bus pass as soon as possible  after cancellation  can i use my current bus pass after the  31st of march 2011  no  however should there be any delays in  dispatching the new bus passes for any  reason essex county council will  publicize information accordingly  if you have any more questions about the  concessionary bus pass scheme please  email transportation at rochford.gov dot  uk  or phone  zero one two six eight  seven  nine eight six zero eight  residents and visitors in north rochford  will now benefit from the introduction  of a new shopper bus service which  started in february  the service route number 174 crouch  village link operates every tuesday and  saturday  leaving from canudan at 9 43 am and 1 47  pm and traveling via south fanbridge the  dome caravan park ashington medical  center and rochford railway station to  tesco south end hospital and south end  central railway station  the return journeys from south end  central railway station leave at 11 50  a.m and 4 p.m  this service has timed stops in the  villages but can be adapted to meet the  needs of the passenger  as long as it's safe to do so the bus  will stop along the route within the  village when hailed  between the 1st of march and the 31st of  october the service will follow the same  route but will start earlier leaving  rochford railway station at 9 00 am  this will include an additional stop at  wallacey island providing access to the  burnham ferry at essex marina which  operates on saturdays  riverside village caravan park and the  wallacy rspb site the return journey  from wallacey island will leave at 104  pm and 5 14 pm  the cost of the journey will be 2 pounds  flat fare single return  children aged 5 to 16 travel half price  and children under 5 travel free if you  hold a concessionary bus pass you will  need to show your pass to receive free  transport  and for any further information please  call zero one seven zero two  five double four double five one or  zero one seven zero two  five four three zero one zero  the tax voucher scheme has ended due to  the reduction in government funding and  budget cuts regressively the council is  no longer in a position to continue to  offer the taxi voucher travel concession  to its residents and the scheme ended on  march 31st  the taxi voucher scheme was introduced  in the district in 2002 to assist those  residents with severe restrictive  mobility  to access essential services at that  time there was no other means of  supporting those residents with their  travel needs  rochford district council was the only  authority in essex to offer this  additional travel subsidy to its  residents however in the last nine years  since the scheme was introduced other  subsidised transport services have now  become available  it was a very difficult decision for the  council to decide to withdraw this  scheme and it is appreciated that users  will now have to make alternative travel  arrangements  taxi drivers will continue to offer the  same level of service to all their  customers however with the ending of the  voucher scheme journeys will no longer  be subsidised by the council  wyvern community transport wct  run services within the district and  offer an excellent door-to-door service  for residents with restrictive mobility  taxi voucher scheme users can find out  more about wct's services by calling  zero one seven zero two  five double four double five one between  nine thirty am and one pm monday to  friday information is also available on  the council's website at  www.rochford.gov dot uk or telephone the  council's transportation department on  zero one two six eight  seven nine 798608

